  "titulo": "The market soared Monday. One giant in your index fund sank.",
  "descripcion": "On Monday, Nov 9, 2026, the S&P 500 rose 2.35% and the Dow added 1,104 points. Nvidia closed 4.27% lower after its board opened an independent investigation into its CEO. Why it matters to index investors: Nvidia is the largest holding in S&P 500 funds, over six percent of the index (8.38% of the SPDR S&P 500 ETF as of Sep 30, 2026). That weight helped funds on the way up and works the same way down. The investigation is ongoing, no finding has been made, and one day of prices proves nothing. Index weights change daily. Not financial advice. Sources: CNBC and The Motley Fool, Nov 9, 2026; State Street SPDR S&P 500 ETF fact sheet.",
